  scuzz check examples/kernel
  scuzz check --message-format=json
"""

def helpBuild(): String =
  """Compile a Scuzz Lang project to a native executable (LLVM)

Usage: scuzz build [OPTIONS] [PATH]

Arguments:
  [PATH]  Project directory containing scuzz.toml [default: .]

Options:
      --message-format <MESSAGE_FORMAT>
          Diagnostic format: human (default) or json (`scuzz check` only) [default: human] [possible values: human, json]
      --out-dir <OUT_DIR>
          Output directory [default: build]
      --full
          Force a full rebuild (ignore incremental fingerprint)
      --verify
          Apply `*.scuzz_sim` / `*.scuzz_drivers` / `*.scuzz_verify` + residual `.require` / `where` (TestRuntime / fuzz graph)
  -h, --help
          Print help

Examples:
  scuzz build
  scuzz build --full examples/hello
  scuzz build --verify examples/counter
"""

def helpRun(): String =
  """Build and run a Scuzz Lang project

Usage: scuzz run [OPTIONS] [PATH]

Arguments:
  [PATH]  [default: .]

Options:
      --headless
          Force Headless UiRuntime (no display needed)
      --message-format <MESSAGE_FORMAT>
          Diagnostic format: human (default) or json (`scuzz check` only) [default: human] [possible values: human, json]
      --out-dir <OUT_DIR>
          [default: build]
      --watch
          Keep running; [ui] hot-reloads the View tree; IO-only kills and reruns on source change
      --script <PATH>
          Inject script path (SCUZZ_UI_SCRIPT); played after the first pump
      --dump <PATH>
          Structural dump path at finish (SCUZZ_FUZZ_DUMP)
  -h, --help
          Print help

Examples:
  scuzz run
  scuzz run --headless
  scuzz run examples/studio
  scuzz run --headless --script examples/studio/build/record.script --dump examples/studio/build/debug.dump examples/studio
  scuzz run --watch --headless

Desktop/Mobile `run` writes build/record.script (live OS input; keys as `key`; auto-repeat as `key a+repeat`; Shift+arrows as `key ArrowLeft+shift`; copy/cut/paste as those verbs; hover and right-click as `hover` / `secondary`) and build/debug.dump. Replay Headless with --script and --dump. `[ui] run --watch` is hot reload. `build/inject.script` stays watch playback only (`dump` / `reload` / `quit` / `resetpeak` / `key` / `compose` / `commit` / `caret` / `select` / `copy` / `cut` / `paste` / `drag` / `hover` / `secondary` included). Desktop quit is window close. Headless `quit` stops the session.
"""

def helpFuzz(): String =
  """Search in-source properties, drivers, and [taps] events under TestRuntime; mix coverage-guided search and mutation

Usage: scuzz fuzz [OPTIONS] [PATH]

Arguments:
  [PATH]  [default: .]

Options:
      --iterations <ITERATIONS>
          Iteration budget. Search then mutation. `0` replays corpus/ only [default: 32]
      --message-format <MESSAGE_FORMAT>
          Diagnostic format: human (default) or json (`scuzz check` only) [default: human] [possible values: human, json]
      --seed <SEED>
          Deterministic LCG seed [default: 42]
      --replay <REPLAY>
          Replay a repro.toml (events + optional schedule_seed / pct_d / pct_k + optional fault_seed)
      --oracles
          Mutate residual Property.check / Property.assert / .require predicates
      --no-fail-fast
          Finish search and still mutate after the first search failure
      --minimize-corpus
          Greedily minimize corpus/*.toml entries (keep pass/fail + declared sometimes coverage), then exit
      --relate
          Judge (Timeline, Timeline) => Verdict relation claims: replay each corpus entry under its own and a perturbed schedule, then exit
  -h, --help
          Print help

Examples:
  scuzz fuzz --iterations 16
  scuzz fuzz --iterations 16 examples/counter
  scuzz fuzz --iterations 0
  scuzz fuzz --oracles examples/counter
  scuzz fuzz --replay build/fuzz/repro.toml
  scuzz fuzz --minimize-corpus
  scuzz fuzz --no-fail-fast --iterations 8 examples/bad-example

`scuzz fuzz` loads `<pkg>/corpus/*.toml` (sibling of goldens/) and replays those entries before search. `--iterations 0` is corpus-only: replay, then stop. A missing or empty corpus/ is a no-op. `examples/bad-example` is an expected fuzz failure (known-wrong `bump`). `examples/bad-fault` is an expected fuzz failure (swallowed `Fs.write` under a fault seed). `examples/bad-adt` is an expected fuzz failure (wrong `record` area). `examples/bad-sched` is an expected fuzz failure (lost Queue offer order under PCT). `examples/bad-intent` is an expected check failure (empty `*.scuzz_verify`). `examples/bad-split` is an expected fuzz failure (silent live/verify dump mismatch). Default stops at the first search failure. `--no-fail-fast` finishes search and still mutates. `scuzz check` and `scuzz test` still pass on the other expected-fail packages.
"""

def helpNew(): String =
  """Create a new Scuzz Lang project

Usage: scuzz new [OPTIONS] <NAME>

Arguments:
  <NAME>  

Options:
      --message-format <MESSAGE_FORMAT>
          Diagnostic format: human (default) or json (`scuzz check` only) [default: human] [possible values: human, json]
      --path <PATH>
          [default: .]
      --ui
          Scaffold a Headless UI sample instead of an IO hello
  -h, --help
          Print help

Examples:
  scuzz new mycli
  scuzz new myapp --ui
  scuzz new myapp --ui --path /tmp
"""

